From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grigory Tuboltsev <gtubolcev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:00:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] appearance: Add a schedule to switch the style at set
 times

Add a "Schedule" tab to the appearance dialog holding any number of rules
"at HH:MM switch the style". Each rule can, together or separately:

- set the Gtk theme: the dark or light variant of the theme in use at the
  time of the switch (looked up case-insensitively, e.g. Greybird ->
  Greybird-dark, Orchis-Compact -> Orchis-Dark-Compact) or a fixed theme;
- set the color scheme (GSettings org.gnome.desktop.interface color-scheme,
  read via the settings portal by GTK 4/libadwaita, Qt 6, Firefox, Chromium);
- set the matching Xfwm4 theme (default follows /Xfce/SyncThemes), the icon
  theme or the cursor theme, and run a shell command ("More..." dialog).

Rules are stored in the xsettings channel under /Xfce/ThemeSchedule/ as
parallel string arrays and applied by a new xfsettingsd helper, so they work
while the dialog is closed. A rule fires when the clock crosses its time;
a setting changed by hand stays until the next rule, and a switch missed
while logged out is made at login.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
